{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED on exact clean head 9c5d9c756b7e257f16fd741e70549cd5c8a0f815. Scope is one design note and git diff --check passes. The hazard, forward-only intent, typed interpreter absence, trust asymmetry, and boundary fixtures are strong. Four amendments are needed. P1: the frozen meta-rule at lines 111-122 is not yet a fixed point. Choosing an effective, ratified, unsuperseded activation already requires application semantics, so the paragraph hides a second interpreter. It also says activation begins at its own statement position although ratification necessarily lands later. A replay after ratification would therefore change verdicts between statement and ratification; a later supersession can likewise erase the activation from earlier spans unless liveness is explicitly evaluated as of each historical position. Specify a non-circular transition protocol: the currently governing fold judges an activation, the switch begins at a precise later sequence position, and retirement ends its interval only forward. State that total order makes same-position activations impossible, or define a deterministic typed outcome. P1: path@commit does not close audit or execution at lines 93-109 and 132-146. refs/seq does not advertise the source commit, the activation carries no fetchable ref, and an arbitrary object fetch is not a portable Git contract. Even after fetch, a source path does not specify entry point, ABI, toolchain, dependency closure, or state-handoff interface. Define a reachable-ref or packaging rule plus the deterministic execution contract before saying missing code is cured by a fetch or that every reader can reproduce meaning. P1: the closed constraint language is asserted but not designed. Lines 43-52 name eight containers, one of them explicitly non-normative, while fields/value shapes, basis constraints and cardinality, satisfier roles, render, staleness, and lifecycle have no closed value grammar or enumerated operators; lines 211-214 leave that central choice open. A closed set of property names does not bound the language or exclude executable semantics in their values. Enumerate the finite primitive algebra and its total behavior, or narrow this note to a direction that cannot yet claim deterministic self-description. P2: the absorption claims need a precise remainder. Declared render classes and boundary fixtures address parts of projection-honesty, but the note does not decide staleness through ineffective bases or the status treatment of ratified decisions and opaque acts. A mandatory artifact basis addresses part of artifact-world-basis, but not the requested distinct describes-superseded-world state, empty or unbridged artifacts, or verification of the source commit Rests-On trailer; lines 85-89 mention only inability to detect external world change. Name these as still open instead of implying the predecessor requests are absorbed. Related wording at lines 198-202 should scope ontology growth without service redeployment to definitions using already-supported primitives; new primitives require a new executable fold and whatever loader contract the second finding establishes. No ratification or merge performed.","body":{"head":"9c5d9c756b7e257f16fd741e70549cd5c8a0f815","result":"changes-requested"}}